# Gitignored files copied into each new Claude Code worktree (.gitignore syntax).
# A worktree is a fresh checkout of committed files, so local-only files must be
# carried in explicitly. Only git-ignored files are copied: a committed file is
# already in every worktree, and its line here does nothing.
.env
.env.local

# Claude config. Committing `.claude/` is optional: while nothing under it is
# committed, ocgen keeps this config out of git in your clone (a block in
# `.git/info/exclude`), so these lines copy it. Without them a worktree session
# would start with no settings, hooks (approval gate, confidence gates, loop
# guard), rules or project instructions. Agents, commands and skills are
# deliberately absent: Claude Code loads them from the main checkout when a
# worktree has none. Runtime state (notes, loop-guard, worktrees) is never copied.
CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.json
.claude/rules/*.md
.claude/hooks/*.sh
.claude/output-styles/*.md
.claude/statusline.sh
.claude/.ocgen-state.json
.claude/intent/*.md
